From 6690d890c280fbd220578bbfdebb9309defa44d8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: scada <scada@noreply.codeberg.org>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 21:06:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 47/53] Revert the 2 s glink intent timeout: the ADSP needs ~20
 s to come up

v19 waited 10 s for an intent and its first ADSP QMI completed at 26.9 s,
with no glink errors and wlan0 up. v27 shortened the wait to 2 s; its
first SLIMbus QMI now fails at 16.3 s (slim-ngd-ctrl: QMI TXN wait fail:
-110), then qcom_sysmon reports "timeout waiting for subsystem event
response" and every later APPS->ADSP message fails with "intent request
timed out" forever, so the ADSP is unusable: no WLAN QMI, no wlan0, and
the modem eventually crashes with "RCECB client callback runtime
exceeded". The ADSP firmware simply needs longer than 2 s to initialise
its glink channels after the remoteproc comes up.

Go back to the 10 s wait. A healthy ADSP grants an intent in
milliseconds, so the 10 s ceiling only matters while it is still booting.
---
 drivers/rpmsg/qcom_glink_native.c | 10 +---------
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 9 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/rpmsg/qcom_glink_native.c b/drivers/rpmsg/qcom_glink_native.c
index 4bc4dadd87c2..2854de7e6b93 100644
--- a/drivers/rpmsg/qcom_glink_native.c
+++ b/drivers/rpmsg/qcom_glink_native.c
@@ -213,14 +213,6 @@ static const struct rpmsg_endpoint_ops glink_endpoint_ops;
 #define GLINK_CMD_RX_DONE_W_REUSE	14
 #define GLINK_CMD_SIGNALS		15
 
-/*
- * How long a sender waits for the remote to grant an intent. A remote that
- * answers does so in milliseconds; joan's ADSP firmware never answers, and a
- * 10 s wait per message there stalled the sysmon notifications of a modem
- * boot past the modem's own initialisation watchdog.
- */
-#define GLINK_INTENT_REQ_TIMEOUT	(2 * HZ)
-
 #define GLINK_FEATURE_INTENTLESS	BIT(1)
 
 #define NATIVE_DTR_SIG			NATIVE_DSR_SIG
@@ -1463,7 +1455,7 @@ static int qcom_glink_request_intent(struct qcom_glink *glink,
 				 (READ_ONCE(channel->intent_req_result) > 0 &&
 				  READ_ONCE(channel->intent_received)) ||
 				 glink->abort_tx,
-				 GLINK_INTENT_REQ_TIMEOUT);
+				 10 * HZ);
 	if (!ret) {
 		dev_err(glink->dev, "intent request timed out\n");
 		ret = -ETIMEDOUT;
-- 
